    "q-113810": {
      "dom_id": "step-q113810",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "The point $P$ with coordinates $(3,-2)$ lies on the curve $y=f(x).$ Which point must lie on $y=-f(x)?$",
      "worked_solution": "The transformation $y=-f(x)$ reflects the curve $y=f(x)$ in the $x$-axis.\n\nFirst, notice that the point $P(3,-2)$ lies $2$ units *below* the $x$-axis. So, under the action of the transformation, this point will be reflected $2$ units *above* the $x$-axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14217907/assets/c20856218b6f5f18c9a3465027a8f1a64a67f2c0d8ef3bd97fba5236f7b81bab.png)\n\nWe conclude that the point $(3,2)$ must lie on the graph of $y=-f(x).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-113810-a",
